 "notes": "U(1)_{B-L} dark photon dark matter search with PPTA DR2 (26 pulsars). Curve is the red dashed 'uncorrelated (26 pulsars)' 95% upper limit from the right panel of Fig.1 (upperlimit.pdf, vector). The paper bounds the dimensionless coupling epsilon normalized to the EM coupling e (Eq.2: a ~ eps*e*(q/m)...); converted to the U(1)_{B-L} gauge coupling via g_BL = e*sqrt(epsilon^2) with e=sqrt(4*pi*alpha)=0.30282. Plot y-axis is epsilon^2; x-axis is m_A in eV (calibrated from major tick marks). The uncorrelated analysis (A) is performed over the full plotted mass range; the correlated (solid) curve is only done for m_A<=1e-22 eV and nearly coincides at the lowest masses but is up to ~1 order higher at 1e-22 eV. The paper states the true (hybrid) result lies between the correlated and uncorrelated cases. Sharp spike near m_A~1e-22 eV (f~2.4e-8 Hz) is a real feature of the limit. Local DM density rho0=0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed (|A0|^2=2*rho0/m_A^2); not rescaled. A U(1)_B result is also presented (left panel) but only VectorBL is in the schema.",
